{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 42, :comments ["<b>Eliyasaf son of De'uel.</b> It alludes to the fact that they were gathered to their cities beforehand by the word of HaShem as stated — unlike the mighty warriors who crossed over, every armed man, etc. — and this is the verse saying <b>el yasaf</b>. Further, according to the words of the Sages of blessed memory, the land of Sihon and Og was not included in the gift of the land of Israel that HaShem gave to Abraham, as they said in Sifrei (part 2, pisqa 299), and this is their language: ״excluding the other side of the Jordan that you took on your own״ — thus far. And we find that the land of Israel has its own legal status (Shevi'it 9:2) as is known; and see what I wrote in parashat Matot at the verse ״עֲטָרוֹת״ etc. Therefore he was called <b>Eliyasaf</b>, because he added to take more than the gift of HaShem, and HaShem agreed with them. <b>Son of De'uel</b> — meaning that they made an acknowledgment as testimony to know that they are known as servants of El, all the tribes of Israel alike, as stated in Joshua (22:27, 22:34)."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "The Hebrew text reads <b>אֶל יָסָף</b> as two words, riffing on the name אֶלְיָסָף (Eliyasaf = 'El will add'); both forms are rendered literally to preserve the wordplay."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:06:42.623738734Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}